.TH HC91EMU 1 "June 2026" "hc91emu" "HC-91 Emulator Manual"
.SH NAME
hc91emu \- emulator for the I.C.E. Felix HC family of ZX Spectrum\-compatible computers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hc91emu
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file .tap|.tzx|.wav|.sna|.z80|.szx|.scr|.rzx]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hc91emu
emulates the Romanian I.C.E. Felix HC home computers \(em primarily the
.B HC\-91
(a ZX Spectrum 48K\-compatible machine), plus the HC\-85, HC\-90, the
128K\-class
.B HC\-128
(banked RAM and AY\-3\-8912 sound) and the
.B HC\-2000
(floppy disk interface with CP/M 2.2).
.PP
The emulator is cycle\-exact: per\-M\-cycle memory and I/O contention,
beam\-accurate video (mid\-frame border effects and multicolour render
correctly), floating bus, the undocumented Z80 behaviors (MEMPTR, the
Q register, interrupted block instructions), exact tape pulse timing
and a 50 Hz drift\-free frame interrupt.
.PP
It runs in two modes: a scriptable
.B headless
mode (the default) intended for automation and testing \(em screenshots,
screen OCR, typed input at given frame numbers, WAV recording \(em and an
interactive
.B SDL2
mode
.RB ( \-\-sdl )
with live video, beeper/AY audio, host keyboard and game controller
support. The SDL frontend loads the SDL2 runtime with
.BR dlopen (3),
so building the emulator needs no external dependencies at all.
.PP
A single optional positional argument names a file to attach or load,
dispatched by extension: tape images
.RB ( .tap ,
.BR .tzx ,
or a sampled
.B .wav
recording of a real cassette),
snapshots
.RB ( .sna ,
.BR .z80 ,
.BR .szx ),
a raw screen
.RB ( .scr )
or an RZX input recording
.RB ( .rzx ).
.SH MACHINES
Selected with
.BR \-\-machine :
.TP
.B hc91
The default. 48K Spectrum\-compatible; the genuine ROM differs from the
Sinclair 48K ROM in 50 bytes (banner and a CP/M bootstrap). Port 0x7E
bit 0 pages a separate low 16K RAM bank over the ROM (the CP/M mode
entered by \fBRANDOMIZE USR 14446\fP).
.TP
.B hc85, hc90
Banner variants of the same 48K machine (genuine ROM dumps).
.TP
.B 48k
The standard Sinclair ZX Spectrum 48K ROM.
.TP
.B hc128
HC\-91\-derived machine with 128K RAM banked through port 0x7FFD (banks
0\-7 at 0xC000, shadow screen in bank 7, ROM select, lock bit; odd banks
contended) and an AY\-3\-8912 PSG at ports 0xFFFD (select/read) and
0xBFFD (write), mixed into the audio output. 128K .z80 and .szx
snapshots are read and written; 48K snapshots load into a locked
USR0\-style bank set.
.TP
.B hc2000
48K\-class machine with the HC disk interface: an i8272 floppy
controller (ports 0x85 status, 0x87 data, 0x05/0x07 control latch), an
8K interface shadow ROM with 16K interface RAM, and the system
configuration latch at port 0x7E that can map the CP/M ROM, move the
ROM window to 0xE000, relocate the video generator to 0xC000 and lock
itself. Boots CP/M 2.2 from a system disk image; HC BASIC disks are
served to the IF1\-style BASIC (CAT, LOAD *"d";1;"name").
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BI \-\-machine " M"
Machine model:
.BR hc91 " (default), " hc85 ", " hc90 ", " 48k ", " hc128 ", " hc2000 .
.TP
.BI \-\-rom " FILE"
Override the main ROM image (default chosen per \-\-machine from
.IR roms/ ).
.TP
.BI \-\-rom1 " FILE"
hc128: the second 16K ROM (default: a copy of ROM 0; only one genuine
HC\-128 ROM image is dumped).
.TP
.BI \-\-rom\-if1 " FILE"
hc2000: the disk interface ROM (default
.IR roms/hc2ki1.rom ;
8K images are mirrored into the 16K window).
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " N"
Number of 50 Hz frames to run in headless mode (default 300; 50 frames
= 1 emulated second). Ignored in SDL mode unless \-\-sdl\-frames is used.
.TP
.B \-\-turbo
Accepted for compatibility; the headless mode never paces, so this is
a no\-op.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-floating\-bus
Unattached port reads return 0xFF instead of the byte the ULA is
fetching. (Some software, e.g. Arkanoid, requires the floating bus and
freezes with this option \(em it exists for experiments.)
.SS Display, audio and state output
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " FILE"
Write a PNG of the final frame (320\(mu240: 256\(mu192 paper plus
border).
.TP
.B \-\-text
Print the final screen as 24 lines of 32 characters, OCR'd against the
ROM font. Inverse video is recognized; unknown glyphs print as
.BR ? .
(The HC\-2000 CP/M console uses its own font and is not OCR\-readable;
use screenshots there.)
.TP
.BI \-\-fb\-dump " FILE"
Write the final frame as raw 320\(mu240 RGBA bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-wav " FILE"
Record the beeper (and on hc128 the AY mix) to a 44.1 kHz mono 16\-bit
WAV covering the whole run.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-sna " FILE"
Save a 48K .sna snapshot after the run. (Refused if SP points into
ROM; on hc128 only the current 48K view is stored \(em prefer .z80
or \&.szx there.)
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-z80 " FILE"
Save a .z80 v2 snapshot (uncompressed pages; on hc128 hardware mode 3
with all eight banks, the 0x7FFD latch and the AY registers).
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-szx " FILE"
Save a .szx (zx\-state v1.4) snapshot (on hc128: machine id 2, eight
RAM pages and an AY block).
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-scr " FILE"
Save the raw 6912\-byte screen (pixels + attributes).
.SS Input scripting (headless)
.TP
.BI \-\-type " \(dqSTRING@FRAME\(dq"
Type STRING starting at the given frame using BASIC key mapping
(letters, digits, symbols via SYMBOL SHIFT, \en for ENTER; literal
\(dq\en\(dq in the argument is converted). Keys are held 6 frames with
6\-frame gaps. Repeatable (up to 32). See
.B BASIC KEY TOKENS
below for typing keywords.
.TP
.BI \-\-keys " \(dqFRAME:NAMES\(dq"
Press a raw key chord at the given frame, e.g.
.BR \(dq100:CAPS+1\(dq .
Names: A\-Z, 0\-9, ENTER, SPACE, CAPS (CS, SHIFT), SYM (SS, SYMSHIFT).
Repeatable (up to 32).
.TP
.B \-\-autoload
Schedule typing
.B LOAD \(dq\(dq
+ ENTER at frame 250 \(em the usual way to start .tap/.tzx files.
.TP
.BI \-\-joy " \(dqF\-G:DIRS\(dq"
Hold joystick directions over frames F..G (exclusive). DIRS is a
combination of U, D, L, R, F (fire), e.g.
.BR \(dq300\-480:R+F\(dq .
Routed per \-\-joy\-type. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-joy\-type " T"
Where \-\-joy events go:
.B kempston
(default; auto\-attaches the interface),
.B sinclair
(Interface 2 stick 1, keys 6\-0) or
.B cursor
(keys 5/6/7/8/0).
.TP
.B \-\-kempston
Attach the Kempston interface at port 0x1F. When absent the port
floats authentically (some games probe for this).
.SS Tape
.TP
.B \-\-real\-tape
Disable the instant LD\-BYTES ROM trap and play the tape at pulse level
with exact T\-state timing (required for custom/turbo loaders). The
player auto\-pauses at block boundaries while no loader polls the EAR
port and resumes when loading restarts, auto\-rewinds at the end of the
tape while a loader is still searching, and honors TZX stop\-the\-tape
markers \(em multi\-load and flip\-the\-tape schemes work.
.IP
A
.B .wav
file (a digitized recording of a real cassette) always loads this
way: the samples are DC\-corrected and Schmitt\-triggered into edges,
so \-\-real\-tape is implied. PCM 8\- or 16\-bit, mono or stereo,
4\-192 kHz; silences longer than a second become block boundaries.
.TP
.BI \-\-play\-at " N"
Press PLAY at frame N (default 320 with \-\-autoload, else 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-tape\-b " FILE"
Attach the other cassette side. Swap sides with F8 in SDL or
\-\-swap\-at headless; each swap toggles between the two files, rewound
and paused at the start.
.TP
.BI \-\-swap\-at " N"
Insert the \-\-tape\-b cassette at frame N (headless).
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-tape " FILE"
Capture BASIC SAVE output (the SA\-BYTES ROM trap) as a byte\-exact
\&.tap file. The file is truncated first and blocks are appended.
.SS Disks (hc2000)
.TP
.BI \-\-disk " FILE"
Insert a disk image in drive A (attaches the IF1 interface if needed).
Raw images in the four period geometries are accepted:
655360 (HC BASIC 3.5\(dq 80\(mu2\(mu16\(mu256),
737280 (CP/M 2.2 3.5\(dq 80\(mu2\(mu9\(mu512),
327680 and 368640 (the 40\-track 5.25\(dq variants).
Writes are buffered and written back to the file on exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-disk\-b " FILE"
Drive B image.
.TP
.B \-\-boot\-cpm
hc2000: reset straight into the CP/M boot ROM, which loads CP/M 2.2
from the system tracks of the disk in drive A to the
.B A>
prompt. (The authentic route from BASIC is
.BR "RANDOMIZE USR 14446" .)
.SS Recordings (RZX)
.TP
.BI \-\-rzx\-record " FILE"
Record the session as an RZX input recording: a .z80 of the starting
state plus, per frame, the fetch count and every port\-read byte.
Replaying the file (pass it as the input file) reproduces the run
exactly \(em useful as a whole\-run regression test. Compressed and
foreign RZX files replay too; "protected" ones are rejected.
.SS SDL frontend
.TP
.B \-\-sdl
Open an interactive window (resizable, aspect\-kept) at 50 Hz with
live audio. Needs only the SDL2 runtime library at run time. See
.B SDL CONTROLS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-sdl\-frames " N"
Auto\-quit the SDL session after N frames (used by the test suite).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
Initial window size multiplier, 1\-8 (default 2 = 640\(mu480).
.TP
.B \-\-trace\-frames
Print the frame number and PC to stderr every 50 frames (cheap
progress indicator).
.SS Debugger
All addresses and ports are hexadecimal, with optional \fB$\fP or
\fB0x\fP prefix.
.TP
.B \-\-monitor
Stop in the monitor before the first instruction.
.TP
.BI \-\-break " ADDR"
Set a PC breakpoint (repeatable, up to 32).
.TP
.BI \-\-watch " ADDR"
Memory write watchpoint (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-rwatch " ADDR"
Memory read watchpoint \(em note it also fires on opcode fetches.
.TP
.BI \-\-pwatch " PORT"
I/O watchpoint. Values \(<= 0xFF match the low port byte; larger values
match the full 16\-bit port.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug " \(dqCMD;CMD;...\(dq"
Scripted monitor input: one command is consumed per prompt, then input
falls back to stdin (prompting only on a tty); when both run out the
monitor auto\-continues so headless runs never hang.
.TP
.BI \-\-trace " FILE"
Write a per\-instruction trace: address, disassembly and registers
before execution, plus the running T\-state count. HALT idle cycles are
logged once.
.SH MONITOR COMMANDS
Inside the monitor (entered via breakpoints, watchpoints or
\-\-monitor), addresses are hex and counts decimal; an empty line
repeats the last command.
.TP
.B r, regs
Registers, flags (letters for set bits), frame\-relative T\-state,
frame number and total T\-states.
.TP
.B d, dis [ADDR [N]]
Disassemble N instructions (default 8) from ADDR (default PC; the
names pc, sp, hl are accepted). Full coverage including undocumented
opcodes, DDCB result\-copy forms and relative\-jump targets.
.TP
.B m, mem ADDR [N]
Hex + ASCII dump of N bytes (default 64).
.TP
.B s, step [N]
Execute N instructions (default 1), then stop again.
.TP
.B c, cont
Continue execution.
.TP
.B b, break [ADDR]
Toggle a PC breakpoint; without argument, list breakpoints.
.TP
.B w, watch [ADDR] / wr, rwatch [ADDR] / wp, pwatch [PORT]
Toggle write/read/port watchpoints; without argument, list.
.TP
.B t, trace FILE|off
Start or stop per\-instruction tracing.
.TP
.B q, quit
Exit the emulator immediately (skips end\-of\-run saves).
.TP
.B h, help
Command summary.
.SH SDL CONTROLS
.TP
.B Spectrum keys
Letters, digits, ENTER and SPACE map directly. Shift = CAPS SHIFT,
Ctrl or left Alt = SYMBOL SHIFT. Composed conveniences: Backspace =
DELETE (CAPS+0), Escape = BREAK (CAPS+SPACE), arrows = BASIC cursors
(plain 5/6/7/8 with \-\-joy\-type cursor), and , . ; ' \- = / type the
corresponding SYMBOL SHIFT symbols.
.TP
.B Joysticks
With \-\-kempston (or automatically when a game controller is present),
arrows + right Alt drive the Kempston interface. The first game
controller's d\-pad, left stick and A button map to Kempston too.
.TP
.B Emulator keys
Tab = turbo while held (no pacing); F5 = pause; F6 = tape play/stop;
F7 = rewind tape; F8 = swap cassette side (with \-\-tape\-b);
F2 = quick state save; F4 = quick state load; F11 = fullscreen;
F10 or closing the window = quit.
.TP
.B Quick save slot
F2/F4 use a single .szx slot at
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hc91emu/quick.szx
(default
.IR ~/.local/state/hc91emu/quick.szx ;
.I %APPDATA%\ehc91emu\equick.szx
on Windows), so it works no matter which directory the emulator was
started from.
.TP
.B Drag and drop
Dropping a tape, snapshot, screen or RZX file onto the window loads
it: tapes get a clean reset followed by the usual autoload typing;
snapshots apply on the spot.
.SH BASIC KEY TOKENS
The 48K BASIC keyword entry needed with
.BR \-\-type / \-\-keys :
keywords come from single keys in K mode (start of a statement), e.g.
.B p
= PRINT,
.B j
= LOAD,
.B o
= POKE,
.B t
= RANDOMIZE,
.B x
= CLEAR,
.B s
= SAVE,
.B i
= INPUT.
Extended\-mode words need the EXTEND chord first \(em press
.B CAPS+SYM
(one \-\-keys entry), then the key:
plain
.B o
= PEEK, plain
.B i
= CODE, plain
.B l
= USR; with SYMBOL SHIFT:
.B SYM+O
= OUT,
.B SYM+I
= IN,
.B SYM+Z
= BEEP.
Example \(em poke a value and read it back:
.EX
hc91emu \-\-frames 500 \e
  \-\-type 'o16384,42\en@260' \e
  \-\-type 'p@330' \-\-keys '342:CAPS+SYM' \-\-type 'o16384\en@354' \-\-text
.EE
.SH FILE FORMATS
.TP
.B .tap
Standard tape image. Loaded instantly through the LD\-BYTES trap, or at
pulse level with \-\-real\-tape. Written by \-\-save\-tape.
.TP
.B .tzx
Extended tape image. Supported blocks: 0x10/0x11 (standard/turbo data,
also fed to the instant trap), 0x12/0x13/0x14 (tone, pulse list, pure
data), 0x18 (CSW recording, RLE and zlib Z\-RLE), 0x19 (generalized
data with symbol alphabets and polarity flags), 0x20/0x21/0x22
(pause/stop, groups), 0x24/0x25 (loops), 0x2A (stop if 48K),
0x30\-0x35 and 0x5A (information, skipped).
.TP
.B .sna
48K snapshot, load and save.
.TP
.B .z80
Snapshot, v1/v2/v3 load (including RLE compression and 128K files on
hc128); saved as v2 uncompressed (48K, or 128K with banks/latch/AY).
.TP
.B .szx
zx\-state v1.4, load and save (48K and hc128). Zlib\-compressed RAM
pages in foreign files are decompressed by a built\-in inflater.
.TP
.B .scr
Raw 6912\-byte screen; loading parks the CPU so the picture persists.
.TP
.B .rzx
Input recording; records with \-\-rzx\-record, replays when given as the
input file, then continues as live emulation when the recording ends.
.TP
.B .img, .dsk
Raw floppy images for the hc2000 (sizes listed under \-\-disk).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HC91_FDC_DEBUG
When set, log every i8272 command and result to stderr.
.TP
.B HC91_TAPE_DEBUG
When set, log tape block progression to stderr (pause/resume/rewind
messages are always printed).
.TP
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER, SDL_AUDIODRIVER
Standard SDL variables; set both to
.B dummy
to run the SDL frontend headlessly (used by the test suite).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on bad arguments, missing/invalid files or failed
saves. The monitor's
.B quit
command exits 0 immediately.
.SH EXAMPLES
Boot to BASIC and read the screen:
.EX
hc91emu \-\-frames 250 \-\-text
.EE
.PP
Play a game interactively with sound:
.EX
hc91emu \-\-sdl software/library/platform/jet_set_willy.tap \-\-autoload
.EE
.PP
Load through the real tape loader and screenshot the result:
.EX
hc91emu game.tzx \-\-autoload \-\-real\-tape \-\-frames 9000 \e
        \-\-screenshot game.png
.EE
.PP
A two\-sided multi\-load original (P\-47):
.EX
hc91emu \-\-sdl shooter/p47_side_a.tzx \-\-autoload \-\-real\-tape \e
        \-\-tape\-b shooter/p47_side_b.tzx
# press F8 when the game asks to turn the tape over
.EE
.PP
HC\-128: program an AY tone from BASIC (OUT = EXTEND then SYM+O):
.EX
hc91emu \-\-machine hc128 \-\-frames 1200 \-\-wav ay.wav \e
  \-\-keys '260:CAPS+SYM' \-\-keys '272:SYM+O' \-\-type '65533,0:@284' ...
.EE
.PP
Boot CP/M on the HC\-2000 and list the disk:
.EX
hc91emu \-\-machine hc2000 \-\-boot\-cpm \-\-disk cpm22\-hc.img \e
        \-\-frames 3400 \-\-type 'dir\en@2600' \-\-screenshot cpm.png
.EE
.PP
Record a session and replay it:
.EX
hc91emu \-\-frames 450 \-\-type 'p2+3*4\en@260' \-\-rzx\-record calc.rzx
hc91emu calc.rzx \-\-frames 460 \-\-text        # prints 14 again
.EE
.PP
Debug: break at the ROM init, inspect, single\-step:
.EX
hc91emu \-\-frames 3 \-\-break 11CB \e
        \-\-debug "regs;dis pc 8;mem 5C00 32;step 3;regs;cont"
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I roms/
Genuine HC\-85/90/91/128/2000 ROM dumps and the Sinclair 48K ROM.
When absent (a fresh checkout),
.B tools/get_roms.sh
fetches all twelve from their preservation sources and verifies them
against pinned sha256 checksums
.RB ( "tools/get_roms.sh --verify"
re\-checks offline).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/hc91emu/quick.szx
The F2/F4 quick save slot of the SDL frontend.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hc91emu/roms/
Fallback location for the default ROMs: when a default ROM is not
found relative to the current directory (a source tree), the emulator
looks here.
This is where the Debian package installs the ROMs.
.TP
.I software/library/
The local classic\-game library built by
.IR tools/get_library.sh ,
classified by genre (see its README for the index).
.TP
.I tests/run_tests.sh
The test suite
.RB ( "make test" ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR README.md ,
.IR ROADMAP.md ,
.I docs/manual.pdf
(the full user manual),
.BR groff_man (7).
.SH HISTORY
Written in June 2026 as a dependency\-free C99 emulator; the Z80 core
passes zexdoc/zexall, Patrik Rak's z80full/z80ccf/z80memptr and
162,000 SingleStepTests bus\-level vectors.
